# Librix local configuration. Copy to `.env` and fill in.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# `.env` is gitignored and must stay that way: none of these values are ours to publish.
#
# SERVICE CONSTANTS
#
# author.today encrypts chapter bodies. Reading one needs two constants that its own Android client is
# built with:
#
#   AT_CERTIFICATE   the client certificate string. Sent (SHA-1, uppercase hex) as the
#                    `X-AT-Certificate` header, and used unhashed in the chapter key derivation.
#   AT_CHAPTER_SALT  a fixed 16-character salt, the third field of that derivation.
#
# Without them the app still browses, searches and shows the charts. Chapters download but can't be
# decrypted.
#
# WHERE TO GET THEM
#
#   1. From author.today's own Android APK, where they originate. Unpack it and pull the two strings
#      out of the client.
#
#   2. From https://github.com/OnlyFart/Elib2Ebook (GPL-3.0), which extracted them already. Look in
#      its author.today chapter decoding for the certificate constant and the salt.
#
# See Documentation/ChapterEncryption.md for what the derivation does with them.

AT_CERTIFICATE=
AT_CHAPTER_SALT=

# SIGNING
#
# Needed only to run on a physical device; a simulator build and the UI tests need neither. Signing is
# manual everywhere, so both values are yours rather than something Xcode works out.
#
#   AT_DEVELOPMENT_TEAM          your Apple Developer Team ID (Xcode → Settings → Accounts, or
#                                developer.apple.com → Membership).
#   AT_PROVISIONING_PROFILE_DEV  the name of your development provisioning profile for this app's
#                                bundle id, exactly as it appears in Xcode or on developer.apple.com.
#
# `Scripts/gen-signing.sh` turns these into the gitignored `Local.xcconfig` before every build, and
# `Librix.xcconfig` includes that. Neither file is committed. See README.md → "Signing".

AT_DEVELOPMENT_TEAM=
AT_PROVISIONING_PROFILE_DEV=
